# --- bulk run artefacts -------------------------------------------------------
# We commit the RESULTS (every CSV/JSON: sequences, metrics, novelty verdicts)
# and the STRUCTURES WE USE (runs/*/shortlist-structures/, 28 files, 16MB).
#
# Excluded below: ~111MB of structures for designs we are not submitting, and
# the per-sample PAE archives. Note these CANNOT be regenerated after tonight,
# because the Foundry Docker images live only on the VM and die with it --
# but submission_all.csv preserves all 100 CDRH3 windows plus full heavy and
# light chains, so every sequence-level finding stays reproducible.
# They remain on local disk; push them to the Nebius private bucket if we want
# them to outlive this machine.
runs/*/design/
runs/*/boltz2/
runs/*/subset/boltz2/
runs/*/refold_boltz2/
*_detailed_scores.cbor.gz

# but always keep the result tables and the structures we shortlisted
!runs/*/shortlist-structures/
!runs/*/**/*.csv
!runs/*/**/*.json

# --- analysis output ---
# chai1_replica_features.csv IS committed (2.5MB, 14,721 rows): regenerating it
# means a 25-minute parse of a 487MB archive, so it is cheap insurance.
nebius-runs/
